text But this is a place where I've already spent so much time before.
text ...Until I met her.
text The word "family" conjures up nothing but negative images for me.
text But how do I explain today, then?
text The last day of our break...
text I decided to leave Furukawa's early in the morning by myself so that the family could spend time together without any outsiders around.
text I decided to be considerate to someone else's family.
text Even I think my own actions are strange.
text I want to be with Nagisa.
text In that case, I should've been with her.
text I should've acted selfishly, like I always do.
text But I'm starting to faintly notice something.
text It's not just Nagisa who I like... I'm starting to like the entire Furukawa family.
text I never knew a family could be like that.
text Humans only act according to their self-interests, and families have an unspoken agreement to ignore that fact as they live together.
text ...That's what I used to think anyhow.
text But...
text I feel so calm when I'm with them.
text I feel like I don't want to leave their side to go anywhere else.
text How pathetic, really.
text Me, of all people, affected by family.
